===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|boni|lang=enm}}, probably from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|bon|lang=fro}}, feminine {{term|bonne||[[good]]|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|bonus||good|lang=la}}. See {{term|bounty}}, and compare {{term|bonus}}, {{term|boon}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[gay|Gay]]; [[merry]]; [[frolicsome]]; [[cheerful]]; [[blithe]].
#* [[w:Shakespeare|Shakespeare]]
#*: ''Be you blithe and '''bonny'''''.
#* Sir Walter [[Scott]]
#*: ''Report speaks you a '''bonny''' monk, that would hear the matichime ere he quitted his bowl.''
# {{context|Geordie|lang=en}} [[beautiful|Beautiful]]; [[pretty]]; [[attractive]].

